# Cartesia

Fetch current docs before writing Cartesia code. Model IDs, `Cartesia-Version` dates, and Line CLI flags go stale.

## Docs

- Index: https://docs.cartesia.ai/llms.txt
- Append `.md` to any `docs.cartesia.ai` page for Markdown (example: https://docs.cartesia.ai/use-the-api/api-conventions.md)
- TTS models: https://docs.cartesia.ai/build-with-cartesia/tts-models/latest.md
- STT models: https://docs.cartesia.ai/build-with-cartesia/stt-models/latest.md
- Line: https://docs.cartesia.ai/line/start-building/quickstart.md
- MCP: https://docs.cartesia.ai/tools/ai/mcp.md

## MCP

Prefer the hosted server at `https://mcp.cartesia.ai/mcp` (OAuth via the Playground). Use it to list voices, generate TTS, transcribe, clone, and manage pronunciation dictionaries. Do not treat MCP as a production SDK.

## Language vs locale vs accent

Do not collapse these:

- **language** — coarse code (`en`, `es`)
- **locale** — language-region bucket (`en-US`, `en-GB`)
- **accent** — a specific voice identity inside a locale

One locale can have many accents. `en-US` includes General American and Southern American. Country cannot pick a unique accent. Prefer catalog IDs from the API over display names when the client will persist or send a value back.

## Auth

- Server: `Authorization: Bearer <api_key>` from https://play.cartesia.ai/keys
- Browser/mobile: never embed API keys. Mint a short-lived access token on the backend.
